request.description:
Liveness probe. Returns `{"status":"ok"}` once the GGUF weights have finished loading. Returns 503 while the model is still loading — expected during the ~900 s `start_period` on first launch (initial UD-IQ1_S download is ~176 GB). LLAMA.md § No tests.

#### Schemas

Public (no API key check); `/v1/health` answers the same.

Response `200` (`application/json`) — the model has loaded:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["status"],
  "properties": {
    "status": {"const": "ok"}
  }
}
```

Response `503` (`application/json`) — the model is still loading (first start: the GGUF download too):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "llama-server's OpenAI-style error object (README § API errors)",
  "required": ["error"],
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["code", "message", "type"],
      "properties": {
        "code": {"const": 503},
        "message": {"const": "Loading model"},
        "type": {"const": "unavailable_error"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

OpenAI-compatible model listing. Returns `{"object":"list","data":[{"id":"glm5.2","object":"model",...}]}` where the `id` matches the alias set via `-a` in the compose command (LLAMA.md § Configuration knobs). Use this to sanity-check that the alias the client sends in `"model"` matches what llama-server actually advertises.

#### Schemas

Same as `vllm: GET /v1/models`.

The OpenAI model list, shared by vLLM, llama-server and LiteLLM. A vLLM server lists exactly one model; LiteLLM lists what the calling key may use.

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "vLLM ModelList (open subset); llama-server and LiteLLM send the same envelope",
  "required": ["object", "data"],
  "properties": {
    "object": {"const": "list"},
    "data": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["id", "object"],
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What a request's `model` must be: vLLM's `--served-model-name` (else the HF repo id, as on vllm-qwen-vl), llama-server's `-a` alias, a LiteLLM `model_name`"
          },
          "object": {"const": "model"},
          "created": {"type": "integer"},
          "owned_by": {"type": "string", "description": "`vllm`, `llamacpp`, `openai` (LiteLLM)"},
          "root": {"type": ["string", "null"], "description": "vLLM: the model path or repo"},
          "max_model_len": {"type": ["integer", "null"], "description": "vLLM: `--max-model-len`"},
          "meta": {
            "type": ["object", "null"],
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "description": "llama-server: `n_ctx_train`, `n_params`, `size`, … (null while the model loads)"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

llama.cpp-native server introspection. Returns default sampler params, model alias, model path, embedded chat template, build info, and enabled modalities. Handy for verifying that `--jinja` picked up GLM's chat template (LLAMA.md § Common pitfalls: forgetting `--jinja` gives raw-completion behavior).

#### Schemas

Response `200` (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": [
    "default_generation_settings",
    "total_slots",
    "model_path",
    "chat_template",
    "build_info"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "default_generation_settings": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "description": "The defaults `/completion` starts from: the launch command's sampling flags (`--temp`, `--top-p`, … `--n-predict`)",
      "properties": {
        "params": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "$comment": "llama-server's sampling parameters as /props and /completion report them (README § POST /completion options); a subset",
          "properties": {
            "n_predict": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "-1: no limit (the server's `--n-predict` caps it)"
            },
            "temperature": {"type": "number"},
            "top_k": {"type": "integer"},
            "top_p": {"type": "number"},
            "min_p": {"type": "number"},
            "presence_penalty": {"type": "number"},
            "repeat_penalty": {"type": "number"},
            "stop": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {"type": "string"}
            },
            "max_tokens": {"type": "integer"},
            "samplers": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {"type": "string"}
            },
            "seed": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        },
        "n_ctx": {"type": "integer", "description": "Context per slot: `-c` / `--parallel`"}
      }
    },
    "total_slots": {"type": "integer", "description": "`--parallel`"},
    "model_alias": {"type": "string", "description": "`-a`"},
    "model_path": {"type": "string"},
    "modalities": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "properties": {
        "vision": {"type": "boolean"},
        "audio": {"type": "boolean"},
        "video": {"type": "boolean"}
      }
    },
    "chat_template": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The Jinja template in use (`--jinja`; `--chat-template-file` when set)"
    },
    "chat_template_caps": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true},
    "build_info": {"type": "string", "description": "`b<build>-<commit>`"},
    "is_sleeping": {"type": "boolean"}
  }
}
```

OpenAI-compatible chat completion. Response shape mirrors OpenAI: `{id, object:"chat.completion", choices:[{message:{role,content},finish_reason}], usage:{...}}`. GLM's chat template is applied server-side because the compose command sets `--jinja` — without that flag the roles are ignored and you get raw-completion behavior (LLAMA.md § Common pitfalls). Add `"stream": true` for SSE streaming.

#### Schemas

Same as `vllm: POST /v1/chat/completions`.

The OpenAI Chat Completions subset shared by vLLM, llama-server and LiteLLM: one 200 schema with two branches, the JSON answer and, with `"stream": true`, the payload of every SSE `data:` line (`text/event-stream`). Server-specific fields say whose they are. Errors are the OpenAI error object (the collection's description).

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "OpenAI Chat Completions request: the fields this stack sends (vLLM ChatCompletionRequest has ~70; llama-server and LiteLLM accept the same names)",
  "required": ["model", "messages"],
  "properties": {
    "model": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "vLLM: the `--served-model-name` (any other is a 404, \"The model … does not exist.\"); llama-server: its `-a` alias (not enforced); LiteLLM: a `model_name`, chain alias or `auto`, which it routes on"
    },
    "messages": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "$comment": "OpenAI chat message param",
        "required": ["role"],
        "properties": {
          "role": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "`system`, `user`, `assistant` or `tool` in this stack"
          },
          "content": {
            "anyOf": [
              {"type": "string"},
              {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "$comment": "OpenAI chat content part; the stack sends `text` and `image_url` parts",
                  "required": ["type"],
                  "properties": {
                    "type": {"type": "string", "description": "`text` or `image_url` in this stack"},
                    "text": {"type": "string"},
                    "image_url": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "additionalProperties": true,
                      "required": ["url"],
                      "properties": {
                        "url": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "An http(s) URL the server fetches, or a `data:image/...;base64,` URI"
                        },
                        "detail": {"type": "string"}
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              {"type": "null"}
            ],
            "description": "Text, or a list of content parts (multimodal); null on an assistant message that only calls tools"
          },
          "name": {"type": "string"},
          "tool_calls": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "$comment": "OpenAI tool call (vLLM ToolCall)",
              "required": ["id", "type", "function"],
              "properties": {
                "id": {"type": "string"},
                "type": {"const": "function"},
                "function": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "required": ["name", "arguments"],
                  "properties": {
                    "name": {"type": "string"},
                    "arguments": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "The arguments as a JSON-encoded string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "On an assistant message: the calls it made"
          },
          "tool_call_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "On a `tool` message: the call it answers"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "stream": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "description": "true: a `text/event-stream` of `chat.completion.chunk` payloads"
    },
    "stream_options": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "properties": {
        "include_usage": {"type": "boolean", "description": "A last chunk carries `usage`"}
      }
    },
    "max_tokens": {"type": "integer"},
    "max_completion_tokens": {"type": "integer"},
    "temperature": {"type": "number"},
    "top_p": {"type": "number"},
    "top_k": {"type": "integer", "description": "Not OpenAI; vLLM and llama-server"},
    "min_p": {"type": "number", "description": "Not OpenAI; vLLM and llama-server"},
    "presence_penalty": {"type": "number"},
    "frequency_penalty": {"type": "number"},
    "seed": {"type": "integer"},
    "n": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Choices to sample (the classifier's sampling confidence)"
    },
    "stop": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"type": "string"},
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"type": "string"}
        }
      ]
    },
    "logprobs": {"type": "boolean"},
    "top_logprobs": {"type": "integer"},
    "response_format": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["type"],
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "enum": ["text", "json_object", "json_schema"],
          "description": "`json_object`: the answer is constrained to JSON (llama-server turns it into a grammar)"
        },
        "json_schema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true}
      }
    },
    "tools": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "$comment": "OpenAI tool definition (vLLM ChatCompletionToolsParam)",
        "required": ["type", "function"],
        "properties": {
          "type": {"const": "function"},
          "function": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "required": ["name"],
            "properties": {
              "name": {"type": "string"},
              "description": {"type": "string"},
              "parameters": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "description": "A JSON Schema for the arguments"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "tool_choice": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"type": "string"},
        {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": true}
      ]
    },
    "parallel_tool_calls": {"type": "boolean"},
    "reasoning_effort": {"type": "string"},
    "chat_template_kwargs": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "description": "Not OpenAI (vLLM, llama-server): variables for the chat template. This stack sends `enable_thinking` (Qwen), `reasoning_effort` (the fixed Qwen template; glm5.3-flash takes `low` | `high`) and `reasoning_strength` (muse-glimmer). Through LiteLLM a request's value REPLACES the deployment's, it is not merged"
    },
    "user": {"type": "string"}
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`) — with `"stream": true` the body is `text/event-stream` instead, one `chat.completion.chunk` per `data:` line, then `data: [DONE]`:

```json
